-- Benefits enrollment (seed 86): open enrollment in the HR portal, October 12 to 23 (game days 8 to 19), as Linda's
-- emails say. Pick a medical plan (Basic HMO, Choice PPO, Saver HSA), dental and vision; the new plans start November 1
-- (day 28), and their premiums come out of every paycheck after, before tax. Not submitting gets the Basic HMO with no
-- dental or vision. The 401(k) can change any time (from the next paycheck): the company matches all of it up to 4% of
-- pay, as Linda tells Jun on day 4. The pay stub (gross, taxes, premiums, 401(k), net) is worked out by the engine;
-- heroes.salary_net stays the paycheck with each hero's plans before November (config benefits_now).
-- Also: Linda's email of day 5 and her line in passing no longer say the plan carries over or "thirty days", and
-- Jun's day 15 talk with Linda (d15_expenses turn 5) is about the open enrollment deadline instead of a 6% match
-- (it said three percent and a match up to six, against day 4 and the day 5 pay stub: four percent, a match up to four).
-- The plans table is in db/schema.sql (this CREATE TABLE is the same).
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS plans (id varchar(16) PRIMARY KEY, kind varchar(8) NOT NULL, name varchar(60) NOT NULL, name_ko varchar(60), premium decimal(8,2) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0, deductible int NOT NULL DEFAULT 0, oop_max int NOT NULL DEFAULT 0, copays json NOT NULL, hsa decimal(8,2) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0, note varchar(255), note_ko varchar(255), sort int NOT NULL DEFAULT 0);






